- Vmag is greater than 6.0  
- SpType does not contain "III", "II", or "Ib"  
- Amag is within range of [16.0, 20.0]  
- Plx is within range of [7.0, 20.0]  
- B-V is less than 0.8  
- Vmag is within range of [5.5, 9.0]  

---

10 different conditions for class "1" (giant star):  
- SpType is in [all spectral types containing "III", "II", or "Ib"] (e.g., K0III, B7II, G7III, B1Ib/II)  
- Amag is less than 16.0  
- Plx is less than or equal to 4.0  
- B-V is greater than or equal to 0.9  
- Vmag is less than or equal to 8.5  
- SpType contains "III" or "II" or "Ib"  
- Amag is within range of [13.0, 16.0]  
- Plx is within range of [0.8, 4.0]  
- B-V is within range of [0.9, 1.3]  
- Vmag is within range of [4.0, 8.5]  

---

These conditions align well with the examples, where all stars labeled "1" have spectral types indicating giants or bright giants and lower absolute magnitudes, while those labeled "0" have main sequence spectral types and higher absolute magnitudes.

